<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Product Consulting Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Organizations often seek product consulting when they face uncertainty
                    around product direction, market opportunities, customer needs,
                    prioritization, or execution. Identifying these challenges helps
                    establish a more focused product strategy.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Unclear Product Direction</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Without a clear product vision, teams may work on disconnected
                    initiatives that do not contribute to meaningful business outcomes.
                    Defining a strong product vision and strategic objectives provides
                    direction for future decisions.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Limited Customer Understanding</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Product decisions based on assumptions can result in features that
                    customers do not value. Customer research, interviews, behavioral
                    analysis, and feedback help teams understand actual customer needs.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Poor Feature Prioritization</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Large product backlogs can make it difficult to determine what should
                    be delivered first. Structured prioritization helps teams focus
                    resources on initiatives with strong customer and business impact.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Weak Market Positioning</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Products may struggle to gain traction when their value proposition
                    and differentiation are unclear. Market and competitor analysis can
                    help organizations establish stronger positioning and messaging.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Execution and Resource Constraints</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Even strong product strategies can fail when resources, capabilities,
                    timelines, or technical requirements are not properly considered.
                    Consulting can help align strategic priorities with realistic
                    execution plans.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Difficulty Measuring Product Success</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Organizations need meaningful metrics to understand whether product
                    investments are producing the expected outcomes. Defining appropriate
                    KPIs provides visibility into customer, product, and business
                    performance.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
